@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.5.2
@changelog
  - Codename: It was never the firmware
  - REAPER could be killed outright by a plug-in whose parameter values print long text. The UF1 display line counted its lengths in a type that cannot go below zero, so a value as long as the whole line wrapped the arithmetic and the resulting error reached REAPER, which treats one as fatal. SSL's own strips never hit it; FabFilter does, which made it look like a compatibility problem.
  - The surface tick now catches an unexpected error instead of letting it end the session.
  - Windows: the driver installer did nothing from the second press onwards. It wrote its signed catalogue into the folder it was hashing, so every run after the first failed before installing anything, with the window closing too fast to read. Pressing again is what people do when nothing happens, so anyone who did was locked out.
  - Windows: each press also added another copy of the driver package to the store while uninstall removed only one. Uninstall now removes every copy.
  - Windows: the install says what happened instead of "started": installed, failed with a log path, or cancelled at the permission prompt. Settings, About also shows what each device is bound to right now, with a Refresh button.
  - Windows: the button says UF8, UC1 and UF1. It always bound all three. After a successful install the devices move to "Universal Serial Bus devices" in Device Manager and are renamed, which the text now says.
  - Names on the surface were still cut to 7 characters in seven places after the colour-bar zone grew to 12, including the Learn-HUD rename and the shared parameter name when set from the UF8.
  - UF1: the EQ graph follows a channel change again, whether you use SEL or the channel encoder. Choosing a channel by hand now outranks the plug-in instance you last activated.
  - UF1: in Extender mode SEL selects the track the fader is on, which is the track its lamp has always reported.
  - UF1: the EQ graph redraws after the device is unplugged and back.
  - UF1: the Learn-HUD's UF1 tab shows the name of the plug-in the UF1 is on, not the Channel Strip's.
  - UF1: umlauts on the panel came out as two characters each.
  - UF1: the Extender's small display named the selected track instead of the track under the fader; an envelope jog left nothing to undo; a long parameter name overflowed an FX-Learn cell identifier; "Fill: Replace" is capped on plug-ins with hundreds of parameters.
